The printing in the box is being used
as commentary only in this case.

00:48:38.900 --> 00:48:42.221
The box is slightly too large,
so we may change its size.

00:48:44.730 --> 00:48:48.127
Then, draw a flow from
the connector to the box.

00:48:50.513 --> 00:48:55.470
Attach a decision element to the box,
and draw a flow from it to scan.

00:48:56.960 --> 00:49:00.550
We then erase the flow-
&gt;&gt; Okay so this is about 1968 or so.

00:49:02.050 --> 00:49:07.700
Again on a big room sized mainframe,
with one guy.

00:49:07.700 --> 00:49:12.731
But, this system really, you could ask
your question even more about this.

00:49:12.731 --> 00:49:16.728
This system was [LAUGH] one of the best
systems I've ever used in every.

00:49:16.728 --> 00:49:19.530
It felt so intimate, it was so
different from the mouse.

00:49:20.650 --> 00:49:25.290
It was one of the things
that we actually looked at.

00:49:27.308 --> 00:49:31.250
I guess I do have to
show the next thing here.

00:49:33.240 --> 00:49:36.820
Just so you think that VR
wasn't something done recently.

00:49:36.820 --> 00:49:39.800
But the second thing Ivan
did after he came back,

00:49:39.800 --> 00:49:42.790
the thing that when it came
back from Arpo was to do these.

00:49:42.790 --> 00:49:45.190
I worked on this one when
I was a graduate student.

00:49:45.190 --> 00:49:48.060
You could grab things and have
the thing in your hand, grab things and

